## 1. Scope

This reference covers GPO-3, the NEMA designation for a flame retardant unsaturated polyester glass mat laminate, known as UPGM203 in IEC and European practice. It is usually specified where flame rating and tracking resistance matter more than mechanical strength.

## 2. Construction

- Glass fibre mat impregnated with an unsaturated polyester resin system with flame retardant fillers.
- Produced as a rigid flat sheet, then machined into barriers, supports and spacers.
- Tracking and flame performance are grade properties, and both are declared.
- Thickness tolerance is controlled at the press rather than after machining.

## 3. Typical specification range

| Parameter | Typical value | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Grade | NEMA GPO-3, IEC designation UPGM203 | Declare the grade on the accompanying documents. |
| Flame behaviour | UL 94 V-0 typical for this grade | One of the main reasons GPO-3 is selected over a general purpose laminate. |
| Tracking resistance | Declared CTI per IEC 60112 | Relevant for barriers close to energised parts. |
| Arc resistance | Declared per ASTM D495 | Relevant where an arc can terminate on the surface. |
| Form | Sheet, or machined parts to drawing | Machining is usually carried out by the same supplier as the sheet. |

Values above describe what is commonly specified for this component class. Confirm the exact figure against the datasheet for the grade being purchased before design release.

## 4. Selection and sizing

- Whether flame rating or mechanical strength is the controlling requirement, which decides GPO-3 against FR4 or G10.
- Tracking and arc resistance requirements, both of which should be declared rather than assumed.
- Thickness and its tolerance, which affect both insulation distance and mechanical fit.
- The machining operations required, since drilling and routing produce dust and burrs.
- Whether certification documents are needed with the shipment.

## 5. Standards commonly specified

- NEMA LI 1, industrial thermosetting laminated products, which defines the GPO-3 grade.
- IEC 60893 series, rigid laminated sheets based on thermosetting resins.
- UL 94, flammability of plastic materials.
- IEC 60112, determination of comparative tracking index.
- ASTM D495, high voltage low current dry arc resistance.
- ASTM D229, test methods for rigid sheet and plate materials.

Standards are listed as those normally cited for this component class. They describe the requirement, not a claim of certification. Test evidence applicable to a specific order is confirmed per purchase order.

## 6. Handling and installation

- Extract dust when machining. Glass filled laminate dust is abrasive and a respiratory hazard.
- Deburr drilled holes and routed edges. A burr on a barrier reduces the effective insulation distance.
- Do not stack machined parts unprotected, since edges chip.
- Store flat and dry. A sheet that takes up moisture changes dimensions slightly before machining.

## 7. Failure modes and mitigation

| Failure mode | Likely cause | Mitigation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Barrier fails clearances because of burrs | Machined edges left undeburred | Deburr and inspect machined edges as part of the process. |
| Tracking on a contaminated surface | CTI below the requirement for the service condition | Specify a grade with a declared CTI for the application and clean before assembly. |
| Thickness out of tolerance | Sheet tolerance not confirmed at incoming | Verify thickness at incoming against the requirement. |
| Missing certification documents | Grade or batch not declared with the shipment | Require grade and batch identification with the delivery. |

## 8. Typical applications

- Switchgear and controlgear barriers and phase separators.
- Busbar supports and spacers in panel builds.
- Transformer and panel builder insulation parts.
- EV charging equipment where a flame rated barrier is required.

